      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When they bring up the environment, immediately pivot the conversation to economic reality, arguing that job security and local prosperity are the *real* priorities for your community. You can state that the current regulations are an overreach that sacrifices immediate economic stability for speculative future environmental gains. Furthermore, you should point out that the regulations fail to account for the existing economic realities of small businesses, making the environmental goal unattainable without crippling the local economy.",
